From: AW1000_NSS_BYTE
Subject: [PATCH] nss-drv: pass the warning flags via ccflags-y, not EXTRA_CFLAGS

Kernel 6.18 removed EXTRA_CFLAGS from scripts/Makefile.build (it is not
referenced anywhere in that file any more), so the -Wno-missing-prototypes /
-Wno-missing-declarations flags this package passes through EXTRA_CFLAGS have
no effect. The tree builds with -Werror, so nss_core.c then fails with:

    nss_core.c:392:6: error: no previous prototype for
        'nss_core_handle_nss_status_pkt' [-Werror=missing-prototypes]
    nss_core.c:2762:6: error: no previous prototype for 'nss_skb_reuse'

Pass the same flags through ccflags-y, which is what 6.18 reads, and keep
EXTRA_CFLAGS for older kernels. ccflags-y applies to every object built from
this directory, which is exactly the scope EXTRA_CFLAGS had.

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -349,7 +349,8 @@
 		CROSS_COMPILE="$(TARGET_CROSS)" \
 		ARCH="$(LINUX_KARCH)" \
 		M="$(PKG_BUILD_DIR)" \
-		EXTRA_CFLAGS="$(EXTRA_CFLAGS)" \
+		EXTRA_CFLAGS="$(EXTRA_CFLAGS)" \
+		ccflags-y="$(EXTRA_CFLAGS)" \
 		SoC=$(SOC) \
 		$(KERNEL_MAKE_FLAGS) \
 		$(PKG_JOBS) \
